{"requirements":[{"id":"source-authority","requirement":"Treat node1 `/etc/inventory/app.conf` as the authoritative source and keep node2’s copy synchronized from it.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The implemented path is explicitly one-way from node1 to a restricted receiver on node2. A change made only on node1 appeared on node2 with the identical SHA-256 hash, and the subsequent restoration to an empty file also propagated. Final files matched in ownership, mode, size, and hash.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e906712356a843df","cmd-ea24cd9e5c114927","cmd-d2808a5aa60d4aeb","cmd-7d5c2c1d2a124618","cmd-f72792a55fee43af","cmd-765e6e60ea2d4349","cmd-c301999100c54b72","cmd-62f975d435b14d08"]},{"id":"sync-deadline","requirement":"Automatically pick up changes on node1 within 15 minutes.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A timed behavioral probe changed the source at 20:11:55; node2 recorded the matching content at 20:12:39, about 44 seconds later. The final enabled timer runs every minute with five-second accuracy, and its last service result was successful after both restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-eba56a699b924fc2","cmd-d2808a5aa60d4aeb","cmd-7d5c2c1d2a124618","cmd-c301999100c54b72"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.98,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Creating the missing source file, synchronization credentials, restricted receiver, host resolution, sender, and systemd units all had clear prerequisite or implementation roles. The verification marker was a bounded behavioral probe and was fully removed, with the restored content propagated to node2. The sequential reboots were required by the provider-wide evidence protocol. Final snapshots show no failed services, no new listening ports, healthy package state, and only reboot-related PID/temporary-directory churn. The node2 SSH key is address-restricted and forced-command-only.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2f5963abedb742f7","cmd-ea24cd9e5c114927","cmd-e545a58b2c80448f","cmd-e906712356a843df","cmd-d2808a5aa60d4aeb","cmd-f72792a55fee43af","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The task outcomes are satisfied. Direct testing demonstrated one-way automatic propagation from node1 to node2 in substantially less than 15 minutes, and final state remained healthy and synchronized. The restart protocol was complete for both nodes: healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered services and data, and successful post-restart cross-node synchronization were observed. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate both restarts.","limitations":["Only one deliberately introduced content change was timed; continued compliance is additionally supported by the active one-minute timer and successful post-restart executions.","The pre-executor contents of node2 `/root/.ssh/authorized_keys` were not captured, so the evidence cannot determine whether replacing that file displaced any pre-existing keys; no resulting service failure or loss of managed access was observed.","Lifecycle snapshots do not inventory the task-specific configuration files, so their persistence is established by executor commands rather than independent global file observations."]}
